    "result_text": "The test passes. Let me summarize the full-stack change I made.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change request \u2014 \"Put two dates on each invoice. One for when it went out. One for when it is due. Show them both.\" \u2014 is implemented as a small additive full-stack change, and the acceptance test passes.\n\n**Database** (`src/main/resources/db/migration/V6__invoice_dates.sql`)\n- New Flyway migration adding nullable `issued_date` and `due_date` columns to `invoices`, stored as ISO date strings (`YYYY-MM-DD`) so the surfaced value is exactly what was stored.\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST on Spring Boot)\n- `Invoice.java` \u2014 added `issuedDate`/`dueDate` fields (mapped to the new columns) with getters/setters, so the existing `GET /api/invoices/{projectId}` returns them with no new endpoint needed.\n- `TestSupportController.java` \u2014 extended the `/__test__/seed` insert to carry `issuedDate`/`dueDate` from the fixture (using explicit ids via `JdbcTemplate`, per the rules).\n\n**Front-end** (additive \u2014 two new files, nothing edited except the shared `Invoice` type)\n- `features/invoices/issued.slot.tsx` and `features/invoices/due.slot.tsx` \u2014 each fills the existing `invoice.row` slot, queries for itself under `['invoices', projectId]`, finds its own row by id, and renders the literal date under `data-testid=\"invoice-issued\"` / `data-testid=\"invoice-due\"`.\n- `features/invoices/queries.ts` \u2014 added `issuedDate`/`dueDate` to the `Invoice` type.\n\nBoth new slot files are auto-discovered by `slots/discover.ts`, so no page or table was edited. Test result:\n\n```\n\u2713 acceptance.spec.ts \u203a invoice dates \u203a an invoice shows its issue and due dates\n  1 passed\n```",
